      "content": "it's just hard to justify the struggle, u know? like, if the end result of everything is just total entropy and nothingness... why is it considered \"right\" or \"good\" to keep fighting it? it feels like we're just fighting a losing battle against the laws of physics. is there actually any logical reason to keep pushing through the pain when the outcome is already decided?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
